  {
   "text": "The Toungoo dynasty was the ruling dynasty of Burma from the mid-16th century to 1752.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "1752",
   "date": "1752",
   "approximate": false,
   "actor": "subject",
   "actor_name": "Toungoo dynasty",
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tabinshwehti and Bayinnaung succeeded in reunifying the territories of the Pagan Kingdom for the first time since 1287.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "1287",
   "date": "1287",
   "approximate": false,
   "actor": "subject",
   "actor_name": null,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "The largest empire in the history of Southeast Asia collapsed in the 18 years following Bayinnaungs death in 1581.",
   "chunk": 1,
   "date_text": "1581",
   "date": "1581",
   "approximate": false,
   "actor": "subject",
   "actor_name": null,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#1"
  },
  {
   "text": "Nyaungyan Min and his son , Anaukpetlun , succeeded in restoring a smaller , more manageable kingdom by 1622.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": "1622",
   "date": "1622",
   "approximate": false,
   "actor": "subject",
   "actor_name": null,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1740 , the Mon people in Lower Burma began a rebellion , founding the Restored Hanthawaddy Kingdom.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "1740",
   "date": "1740",
   "approximate": false,
   "actor": "related",
   "actor_name": "Mon people",
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Hanthawaddy armies captured Inwa in 1752 and ended the 266-year-old Toungoo dynasty.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "1752",
   "date": "1752",
   "approximate": false,
   "actor": "related",
   "actor_name": "Hanthawaddy armies",
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Toungoo_dynasty#4"
  },
  {
